From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:06:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 580/580] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini-station: keep the microSD card
 supply on

With VMCH off and the slot empty, the Gemini's card-detect pin GPIO67
reads low whether a card is in or not, also with its pad pull-up
enabled. The vendor driver turns VMCH back on at the end of the slot's
probe and leaves it on with no card, which suggests the card-detect
switch is referenced to that supply.

Keep VMCH on.

Not yet run on hardware.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
index 4711ed3..5366759 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
@@ -567,10 +567,16 @@
  * 3.3 V signalling only, without the 1.8 V switch.
  */
 &mt6351regulator {
+	/*
+	 * The vendor driver turns VMCH back on at the end of the slot's probe
+	 * and leaves it on with no card. With it off, the card-detect pin
+	 * reads low whether a card is in or not.
+	 */
 	mt6351_vmch_reg: ldo-vmch {
 		regulator-name = "vmch";
 		regulator-min-microvolt = <3000000>;
 		regulator-max-microvolt = <3000000>;
+		regulator-always-on;
 	};
 
 	mt6351_vmc_reg: ldo-vmc {
